### Cinema Management System - Admin & User Authentication Test
### Test file for separate admin and user authentication

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### ========================================
### 1. ADMIN AUTHENTICATION
### ========================================

### 1.1 Register Admin (Manual - requires existing admin token or direct DB insert)
### First admin should be created manually in database
### INSERT INTO admin (nama_admin, email, password, createdAt, updatedAt) 
### VALUES ('Super Admin', 'admin@cinema.com', '$2a$10$hashedpassword', NOW(), NOW());

### 1.2 Admin Login
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@cinema.com",
  "password": "admin123"
}

### Save admin token from response
@adminToken = ADM_eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...

### 1.3 Get Admin Profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 1.4 Update Admin Profile
PUT {{baseUrl}}/admin/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nama_admin": "Super Admin Updated"
}

### ========================================
### 2. USER AUTHENTICATION
### ========================================

### 2.1 User Register
POST {{baseUrl}}/user/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@test.com",
  "password": "user123",
  "nama_pelanggan": "Test User"
}

### Save user token from response
@userToken = USR_eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...

### 2.2 User Login
POST {{baseUrl}}/user/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@test.com",
  "password": "user123"
}

### 2.3 Get User Profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/user/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 2.4 Update User Profile
PUT {{baseUrl}}/user/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nama_pelanggan": "Test User Updated"
}

### ========================================
### 3. AUTHORIZATION TESTS
### ========================================

### 3.1 Admin accessing admin-only endpoint (should work)
POST {{baseUrl}}/films
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nama_film": "Test Film",
  "durasi": 120,
  "genre": "Action",
  "batas_umur": "13+"
}

### 3.2 User accessing admin-only endpoint (should fail - 403)
POST {{baseUrl}}/films
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nama_film": "Test Film",
  "durasi": 120,
  "genre": "Action",
  "batas_umur": "13+"
}

### 3.3 User accessing user endpoint (should work)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 3.4 Admin accessing user endpoint (should fail - 403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 3.5 No token (should fail - 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/profile

### 3.6 Invalid token (should fail - 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/profile
Authorization: Bearer INVALID_TOKEN

### ========================================
### 4. TOKEN PREFIX VALIDATION
### ========================================

### 4.1 Admin token without ADM_ prefix on admin endpoint (should fail)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/profile
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...

### 4.2 User token without USR_ prefix on user endpoint (should fail)
GET {{baseUrl}}/user/profile
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...

### ========================================
### 5. CROSS-AUTHENTICATION TESTS
### ========================================

### 5.1 Admin token on user-only endpoint (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/payment/order
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tickets": [
    {
      "id_jadwal": 1,
      "id_kursi": 1
    }
  ]
}

### 5.2 User token on admin-only endpoint (should fail)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/films/1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### ========================================
### 6. TOKEN EXPIRY TESTS
### ========================================

### 6.1 Admin token should expire in 4 hours
### Wait 4+ hours and try:
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 6.2 User token should expire in 7 days
### Wait 7+ days and try:
GET {{baseUrl}}/user/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### ========================================
### NOTES:
### ========================================
### - Admin tokens have ADM_ prefix and expire in 4 hours
### - User tokens have USR_ prefix and expire in 7 days
### - Admin tokens contain id_admin field
### - User tokens contain id_pelanggan field
### - No explicit "role" or "type" field in JWT payload
### - Separate JWT secrets for admin and user
### - Cross-authentication is prevented at middleware level
